---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { DOMAIN, SITE, pageTitle, phrases, reasons } from "../data";

const title = pageTitle("Why this name");
const description = "Why waxmy.hair is a premium exact-phrase .hair domain: memory, commercial intent, and a category extension. Price on request from Desert Rich.";
const jsonLd = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebPage", name: title, description, url: `${SITE}/why` };
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/why">
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <p class="text-muted"><a href="/">Home</a> / Why this name</p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-accent">The case</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-5xl leading-none">{DOMAIN}</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-xl">Most names ask a customer to learn a new word. This one uses the sentence they already have.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted">“Wax my hair” is what someone says to a friend, types into a map, or puts in a text. Putting that phrase on .hair does not invent demand. It gives the demand a short address.</p>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4">
      {reasons.map((reason) => (
        <section class="rounded-3xl border border-line bg-surface p-5">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl">{reason.title}</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-muted">{reason.body}</p>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>
    <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-3xl">Language it already shares</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      {phrases.map((phrase) => <li class="rounded-full border border-line bg-surface px-4 py-3">{phrase}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted">Treat those as the vocabulary of the brand, not as guaranteed queries. A domain is a head start on memory and type-in. The site still has to deserve the visit.</p>
    <p class="mt-8"><a class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center text-accent" href="/uses">See where the name fits</a></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
